  "identity": "Black-green graveyard midrange where lands matter IN THE GRAVEYARD rather than on the battlefield. Lluwen, Imperfect Naturalist reads '{2}{B/G}{B/G}{B/G}, {T}, Discard a land card: Create a 1/1 black and green Worm creature token for each land card in your graveyard' - so every self-mill is a Worm counter, Evolving Wilds is a land that puts ITSELF in the yard, and the land discarded to pay the cost joins the count before the ability resolves. After the self-grill the deck runs a SECOND payoff on the same resource: Morcant's Eyes x2 sacrifices for a 2/2 Elf per Elf card in the graveyard, which needs no land in hand, no tap, and no creature surviving a turn cycle. The same graveyard also sizes Moon-Vigil Adherents and Gloom Ripper, and Nameless Inversion is removal that becomes an Elf card in the yard the moment it resolves.",
